"""Render the verified frequency sweep report without re-running hardware."""
import json,pathlib,sys
base=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);dest=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[2]);rows=json.loads((base/'summary.json').read_text());v=json.loads((base/'verification.json').read_text());meta=json.loads((base/'metadata.json').read_text());lookup={r['point']:r for r in rows}
valid=[r for r in rows if r['sinad_db']];best=max(valid,key=lambda r:r['sinad_db']['mean']);worst=min(valid,key=lambda r:r['sinad_db']['mean'])
lines=['# Board #4 — 30 MHz to 6 GHz frequency sweep — 18 November 2026','',f"Measured **{v['measured_points']} of {v['planned_points']} planned frequencies**, retaining **{v['snapshots']} paired measurement snapshots**. **{v['fully_valid_sinad_points']} points** have fully valid SINAD estimates; **{v['points_with_transport_counters']} points** have nonzero cumulative transport counters; **{v['points_with_new_transport_errors']} measurement windows** have new transport errors. Independent verification reconciles all retained statistics and settings.",'','## Setup and scope','',
'Original CaribouLite on pi4g-trixie transmits into board #4 on pi4f-trixie through the existing nominal **90 dB coax link**. Both use RF24 and **1 MS/s**. The transmitter requests **0 dBm** throughout (PA code 12), using the preceding NBFM test signal: 1 kHz tone, amplitude 0.4, deviation setting 2500 Hz. Actual calibrated RF output power was not measured.', '',
'Board #4 software **LED1=A39/LED4/D11 is explicitly held low** before every RX start, with readback and LED0 preservation. The unresolved LED1-high failure is not being retested. Neither FPGA firmware nor hardware was changed. Both receivers/transmitters retune while stopped; TX is stopped before RX retuning. Each point has 2 seconds settling and 5 seconds measurement.', '',
'The base grid is 50 MHz, supplemented with amateur/ISM band anchors, European SRD points, and additional samples around the modem-bypass boundaries at 2385 and 2495 MHz. The first point is 30 MHz. The upper software limit is exclusive: **the last point is 5,999.999 MHz; exactly 6,000 MHz was not measured**. This is a sampled sweep, not a continuous-frequency acceptance test.', '',
'Observed RX settings are 1 MS/s, 160 kHz analog bandwidth and 125 kHz digital cutoff. Observed TX settings are 1 MS/s, 80 kHz analog bandwidth and 125 kHz digital cutoff. Snapshot freshness is checked on each host independently; their monotonic clocks are not compared to each other.', '',
f"Noise squelch closed the audio gate at some original points. **{meta.get('repeated_point_count',0)} affected points were repeated with both squelches disabled**, retaining the original runs and the per-point source selection. The final curves use the open-squelch repeats at those frequencies and the original open-gate data elsewhere. The estimator runs before the gate, so gate closure does not itself explain suppressed readings. It requires a detectable 1 kHz component using a 1 dB reporting criterion; unavailable readings are retained as unavailable, not assigned numeric values.", '', '## Frequency response','',
'![RSSI and SINAD versus frequency, logarithmic frequency axis](baselines/20261118-board4-frequency-sweep/frequency-log.png)','',
'[Linear-frequency plot](baselines/20261118-board4-frequency-sweep/frequency-linear.png) · [Vector logarithmic plot](baselines/20261118-board4-frequency-sweep/frequency-log.svg) · [All measurements CSV](baselines/20261118-board4-frequency-sweep/results.csv)','',
f"The highest point-mean estimated SINAD is **{best['sinad_db']['mean']:.2f} dB at {best['frequency_hz']/1e6:g} MHz**; the lowest is **{worst['sinad_db']['mean']:.2f} dB at {worst['frequency_hz']/1e6:g} MHz**. These extrema are measurements of the complete link, not isolated receiver sensitivity.",'','## Amateur and ISM coverage','',
'Band labels use a Region 1 emphasis, with explicitly labeled Region 2 supplements for 222/915 MHz. National subbands vary. At least three measured frequencies fall in every listed range. European 863–870 MHz SRD coverage is included separately; it is not described as an ITU ISM allocation.', '',
'| Band | Range MHz | Measured / numeric SINAD points | Point-mean RSSI range dBm | Reported point-mean SINAD range dB |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for b in v['band_coverage']:
 xs=[r for r in rows if b['low_hz']<=r['frequency_hz']<=b['high_hz']];rs=[r['rssi_dbm']['mean'] for r in xs];ss=[r['sinad_db']['mean'] for r in xs if r['sinad_db']]
 sr=f'{min(ss):.2f} to {max(ss):.2f}' if ss else 'Unavailable'
 lines.append(f"| {b['name']} | {b['low_hz']/1e6:g}–{b['high_hz']/1e6:g} | {len(xs)} / {len(ss)} | {min(rs):.2f} to {max(rs):.2f} | {sr} |")
lines+=['','[Exact band membership and verification](baselines/20261118-board4-frequency-sweep/verification.json). Band-designation references: [ITU ISM frequencies](https://www.itu.int/net/ITU-R/terrestrial/faq/index.html), [RSGB amateur band plans](https://rsgb.services/public/bandplans/). These labels organize conducted laboratory measurements and do not state national operating permissions.','','## Interpretation and limits','',
'The curves include frequency-dependent TX/mixer output, receiver/mixer gain, coax and attenuator response, noise, distortion and clock/tone offsets. The 90 dB attenuation is nominal and was not calibrated across this range. The 0 dBm value is a requested/model setting, not a measured constant RF level at the coax connector. RSSI is the raw modem register reading; SINAD uses the existing fixed-notch audio estimator. No conclusion about calibrated receiver sensitivity, absolute frequency accuracy, board #4 TX performance, or the cause of the LED dependency follows from these data.', '',
'## Evidence and release','',
f"Run `{meta['run']}`. [Plan, collector/helper sources, summary, hashes and independent verification](baselines/20261118-board4-frequency-sweep/README.md). Full paired snapshots and both hosts’ status, command and backend logs are archived under `build/board4-frequency-sweep-20261118/`. The collector stops both radios on completion or exception. Final release checks are retained separately for both hosts; no receiver-side TX commands are part of the experiment.", '']
if not v['all_points_measured'] or v['failed_points']:lines+=['## Missing points','',f"Acquisition recorded {v['failed_points']} failed points. Consult the failure record before interpreting coverage.",'']
if v['points_with_transport_counters']:lines+=['## Transport qualifications','',f"Nonzero transport counters occurred at {v['points_with_transport_counters']} points. Their absolute and per-window changes are retained in summary.json. A stable inherited counter is distinguished from an event during measurement; these records are not a claim of an entirely error-free acquisition history.",'']
dest.write_text('\n'.join(lines))
